# benilla's own interface, one layer on the stock one (docs/METHOD.md): every file is ours, from
# `assets/ui`, and loads in this order after every `FrameXML.toc` row and before the third-party
# addons. It is listed in no addon list, fires no `ADDON_LOADED` and cannot be switched off; a dev
# build boots without it under `WOW_STOCK_UI=1`. A test names its files, so it does not grow.
#
# Adding a file: list it below and in `the_layer_does_not_grow` (src/ui_script/shipped_xml_tests.rs)
# with its reason; any other entry in `assets/ui` (art, a folder) goes in that test's list too.
# Art path `Interface\Benilla\<path>` reads `assets/ui/<path>.tga`, folders included. A Lua call
# the host feeds follows `benilla-ui/src/script/clock.rs`; its feed system goes in `UiFeed`. The
# event-shape gate checks only names in `reference/1.12-events.tsv`, so a new event needs no row.

## Interface: 11200

# The scroll parts of our options window and script log.
ScrollTemplates.xml
# The Keybindings page's templates and script, which OptionsFrame.xml uses at load.
KeyBindingsPage.xml
# `BenillaOptionsFrame`; its rows read the option globals the stock options windows set.
OptionsFrame.xml
# The ESC menu's era look on the stock `GameMenuFrame`, whose Options rung opens ours.
GameMenuAdapters.xml
# `OpenBackpack` and `CloseBackpack` over every equipped bag, for the vendor and the mailbox.
ContainerFrameAdapters.xml
# The pet page's autocast widgets in the pet action button's proportions.
SpellBookAdapters.xml
# The `/errors` script error log and our slash commands.
ScriptLogFrame.xml
# Our fixes to the stock Lua.
FrameXMLFixes.xml
# The character pane's and inspect window's buttons for the ten Gear Slots only (ADR 0007).
GearSlots.xml
# The Boss Bar: boss1 to boss3 top centre with cast bars and the kill linger (ADR 0013).
BossBar.xml
# The world map's quest, service and dungeon marks: gossip icons and a tooltip (spec #383).
WorldMapMarks.xml
# The Reeling Bar, its Angler badge and its banners (ADR 0018).
FishingReel.xml
# The Fishing Journal window, its bait slot, TOGGLEFISHINGJOURNAL's body and /journal.
FishingJournal.xml
